          "It helps to imagine a weaker case. Suppose regression testing found problems, so that pillar earned, say, 10 points instead of 25. The total would drop by 15 points, to about 81.9, well under 90.0. This shows how the structure protects against a single weakness. A model with excellent answers but unstable behavior across versions cannot be certified, and the score makes that visible.",
          "A common mistake is to read a single composite as the whole truth. The composite is useful for the decision, but the pillar scores tell you where to improve. Another mistake is to treat a high score as permanent. The regression pillar exists because quality can slip over time, so the tower must be refreshed as the system changes.",
