          "The Global Supply Chain Control Tower serves as the unified operational command bridge for multinational manufacturing and distribution enterprises. It integrates physical freight logistics, multi-echelon inventory buffers, production scheduling, and vendor procurement into a closed-loop autonomous operating system. The Control Tower is engineered across four synchronized architectural pillars: Pillar 1: Neural Demand Forecasting & Bullwhip Damping; Pillar 2: Multi-Echelon Safety Stock Optimization & Lateral Transshipment; Pillar 3: Autonomous Fleet Routing & Last-Mile Carbon Abatement; and Pillar 4: Cognitive Sourcing, Contract Auditing & 3-Way Reconciliation.",
          "In Part 1 of this Grand Capstone, we operationalize Pillar 1: The Neural Demand Forecasting & Bullwhip Mitigation Subsystem. This subsystem continuously synchronizes point-of-sale retail consumption across global distribution networks. It executes hierarchical time-series reconciliation across corporate, regional, and distribution center levels, sums the distribution-center forecasts (this lab simply sets hierarchical coherence to True rather than testing it), and applies dynamic damping algorithms to keep the multi-echelon Bullwhip Distortion Ratio at or below 1.25.",
