          "Start with readiness. The lab computes a readiness score weighted by headcount, so a large department counts for more than a small one. The result is 83.7 percent, against a target of 80 percent, so the target is met. This weighting matters, because a simple average would let a small, enthusiastic team hide a big, reluctant one. Also, the lab reports zero circuit-breaker alerts for the 150 agents, which is the second pass condition.",
