          "Welcome to the final capstone, and let us start by saying what an operating system means here. On a computer, an operating system is the layer that lets many programs run together without colliding. The enterprise version in this lesson does the same for a company: it lets many agents, data sources, safeguards and business processes run together. The lesson names four pillars. Today we walk through each one, using the lab output as our evidence.",
          "The first pillar is about agents working together. Think of a customer request that passes through several agents, one for engagement, one for ledger accounting and one for operations. Every time one agent hands the work to the next, there is a risk that the message is lost, delayed or garbled. The orchestration fabric is the set of rules and plumbing that keeps these handoffs reliable. The pillar checks two things: how many handoffs succeed, and how long they take.",
