          "The quiz asks why handoff speed and token budgets matter. A swarm is a chain, and a slow link makes the whole chain slow. If each handoff drifts upward in time, a task that touches many agents can take far longer than a customer will wait. Token budgets matter for money. Every message between agents costs tokens, and without a budget a busy system can spend heavily without anyone noticing. Predictable speed and predictable cost are what let a company plan around a system.",
          "A caution for you as a future leader. A result of four tasks all passing is a small sample, and the lesson speaks of reliable convergence of tasks, which is a stronger claim than any single run can show. Treat the pillar as a clear demonstration of what to measure, namely success rate and latency, and expect real systems to be measured over many thousands of tasks. Next, we look at the data that feeds those agents."
