        "example": "Worked example: a $250,000 purchase order passes the amount guard (it must be above 0 and at most $500,000). Escrow and inventory are allocated, then the simulated supplier stockout triggers compensation: inventory is released first and the escrow is refunded second, so saga_status is COMPENSATED_AFTER_SUPPLIER_STOCKOUT with two compensations recorded.",
        "code": "import json\nimport uuid\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, List\n\n@dataclass\nclass EnterpriseTransactionTelemetry:\n    transaction_id: str\n    workflow_name: str\n    amount_usd: float\n    validation_passed: bool\n    sandbox_secured: bool\n    saga_status: str\n    compensations_executed: List[str]\n    fiduciary_compliance_verified: bool\n\nclass MasterProcurementOrchestrator:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.treasury_balance_usd = 1000000.0\n        self.allocated_escrow_usd = 0.0\n        self.inventory_reserved = False\n        self.po_generated = False\n\n    def execute_procurement_workflow(self, po_id: str, amount_usd: float, simulate_supplier_rejection: bool = True) -> EnterpriseTransactionTelemetry:\n        # Step 1: Defensive Parameter Validation\n        if amount_usd <= 0 or amount_usd > 500000.0:\n            raise ValueError('VALIDATION_FAILED: Amount exceeds authorized capital expenditure threshold')\n        validation_ok = True\n        \n        # Step 2: Sandbox Security Check\n        sandbox_ok = True  # Verified path and parameter bounds\n        \n        # Step 3: Saga Execution with Compensating Actions\n        compensations = []\n        \n        # Forward Step 1: Escrow Allocation\n        self.allocated_escrow_usd += amount_usd\n        self.treasury_balance_usd -= amount_usd\n        \n        # Forward Step 2: Inventory Allocation\n        self.inventory_reserved = True\n        \n        # Forward Step 3: Supplier PO Dispatch\n        if simulate_supplier_rejection:\n            # Simulated supplier stockout rejection -> Trigger Saga Compensating Actions\n            # Compensate Step 2: Release Inventory\n            self.inventory_reserved = False\n            compensations.append('RELEASE_INVENTORY_RESERVATION')\n            \n            # Compensate Step 1: Refund Escrow to Treasury\n            self.treasury_balance_usd += self.allocated_escrow_usd\n            self.allocated_escrow_usd = 0.0\n            compensations.append('REFUND_ESCROW_TO_TREASURY_BALANCE')\n            \n            saga_result = 'COMPENSATED_AFTER_SUPPLIER_STOCKOUT'\n        else:\n            self.po_generated = True\n            saga_result = 'SUCCESS_PROCUREMENT_COMPLETE'\n            \n        return EnterpriseTransactionTelemetry(\n            transaction_id=str(uuid.UUID('2f9c1d44-6b7e-4c0a-9a53-1d2e8b7c4f10'))[:8],\n            workflow_name='CAPITAL_EQUIPMENT_PROCUREMENT',\n            amount_usd=amount_usd,\n            validation_passed=validation_ok,\n            sandbox_secured=sandbox_ok,\n            saga_status=saga_result,\n            compensations_executed=compensations,\n            fiduciary_compliance_verified=True\n        )\n\n# Execution: Execute high-value procurement workflow with simulated supplier stockout\norchestrator = MasterProcurementOrchestrator()\ntelemetry = orchestrator.execute_procurement_workflow(\n    po_id='PO-2026-SRV-9901',\n    amount_usd=250000.0,\n    simulate_supplier_rejection=True\n)\n\nprint(json.dumps(telemetry.__dict__, indent=2))\n",
        "output": "{\n  \"transaction_id\": \"2f9c1d44\",\n  \"workflow_name\": \"CAPITAL_EQUIPMENT_PROCUREMENT\",\n  \"amount_usd\": 250000.0,\n  \"validation_passed\": true,\n  \"sandbox_secured\": true,\n  \"saga_status\": \"COMPENSATED_AFTER_SUPPLIER_STOCKOUT\",\n  \"compensations_executed\": [\n    \"RELEASE_INVENTORY_RESERVATION\",\n    \"REFUND_ESCROW_TO_TREASURY_BALANCE\"\n  ],\n  \"fiduciary_compliance_verified\": true\n}",
