          "why": "Classical RLHF requires four models in VRAM (Actor, Critic, Reference, Reward) and suffers from PPO instability. DPO mathematically derives the closed-form implicit reward, allowing direct training on (prompt, winning, losing) triplets via simple cross-entropy.",
          "explanation": "Classical RLHF requires four models in VRAM (Actor, Critic, Reference, Reward) and suffers from PPO instability. DPO mathematically derives the closed-form implicit reward, allowing direct training on (prompt, winning, losing) triplets via simple cross-entropy."
