          "Air-Gapped Software Supply Chain Management requires specialized air-gap data transfer protocols. Modern software dependencies—including Linux kernel packages, container images, Helm charts, and Python libraries—normally rely on dynamic Internet repositories (PyPI, Docker Hub, GitHub). In an air-gapped enclave, engineering teams implement Secure Data Diodes and Cryptographic Air-Gap Transfer Stations. Software updates and verified open-source model checkpoints undergo multi-stage malware scanning, static source code auditing, and cryptographic hash verification at external quarantine stations before being transferred across the physical air gap on write-once optical media.",
