        "example": "Consider a national central bank deploying a sovereign cognitive engine to analyze confidential inter-bank liquidity settlement queues. The platform cannot connect to any external cloud API. Our Sovereign Node Admission Controller intercepts all deployment requests: validating that container images are signed by the internal Bank Root CA, confirming that host nodes have zero external IP routing tables, and verifying that GPU RDMA interconnects are locked down within the private Faraday enclave.",
        "code": "import json\nimport hashlib\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field, asdict\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Tuple, Optional, Any\n\n@dataclass\nclass SovereignContainerImage:\n    image_uri: str\n    sha256_digest: str\n    developer_signature: str\n    vulnerability_scan_clean: bool\n    air_gap_manifest_id: str\n\n@dataclass\nclass NodeAdmissionVerdict:\n    node_hostname: str\n    is_air_gapped: bool\n    external_network_interfaces_detected: int\n    container_signature_valid: bool\n    admission_status: str # 'ADMITTED_TO_SOVEREIGN_POD', 'REJECTED_SECURITY_VIOLATION'\n    fiduciary_compliance_log: str\n\nclass SovereignClusterAdmissionController:\n    INTERNAL_ROOT_CA_KEY = \"SOVEREIGN-BANK-ROOT-CA-KEY-2026\"\n\n    def verify_image_signature(self, image: SovereignContainerImage) -> bool:\n        expected_sig = hashlib.sha256((image.sha256_digest + self.INTERNAL_ROOT_CA_KEY).encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()\n        return (image.developer_signature == expected_sig) and image.vulnerability_scan_clean\n\n    def evaluate_node_admission(\n        self,\n        hostname: str,\n        interfaces: List[Dict[str, str]],\n        image: SovereignContainerImage\n    ) -> NodeAdmissionVerdict:\n        # Check air-gap: Zero public IP or external gateway interfaces\n        external_count = 0\n        for iface in interfaces:\n            ip = iface.get('ip', '')\n            if not (ip.startswith('10.') or ip.startswith('192.168.') or ip.startswith('172.16.') or ip == '127.0.0.1'):\n                external_count += 1\n                \n        air_gapped = (external_count == 0)\n        sig_valid = self.verify_image_signature(image)\n        \n        if air_gapped and sig_valid:\n            status = 'ADMITTED_TO_SOVEREIGN_POD'\n            log = 'Host physically air-gapped and container cryptographically verified by Internal Root CA.'\n        elif not air_gapped:\n            status = 'REJECTED_SECURITY_VIOLATION'\n            log = f'CRITICAL: Host violates air-gap policy! {external_count} external network interfaces detected.'\n        else:\n            status = 'REJECTED_SECURITY_VIOLATION'\n            log = 'CRITICAL: Container image failed cryptographic PKI signature verification.'\n            \n        return NodeAdmissionVerdict(\n            node_hostname=hostname,\n            is_air_gapped=air_gapped,\n            external_network_interfaces_detected=external_count,\n            container_signature_valid=sig_valid,\n            admission_status=status,\n            fiduciary_compliance_log=log\n        )\n\n# Execution: Evaluate sovereign node admission for central bank liquidity model\ncontroller = SovereignClusterAdmissionController()\n\n# Create verified container image\nimg_digest = 'a8f5b2c4e1d3f6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6e7f8a9b0c1d2e3f4a5b6c7d8e9f0a1'\nvalid_sig = hashlib.sha256((img_digest + \"SOVEREIGN-BANK-ROOT-CA-KEY-2026\").encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()\nverified_image = SovereignContainerImage(\n    image_uri='harbor.sovereign.bank.internal/cognitive/liquidity-engine:v2.4.1',\n    sha256_digest=img_digest,\n    developer_signature=valid_sig,\n    vulnerability_scan_clean=True,\n    air_gap_manifest_id='MANIFEST-AG-9901'\n)\n\n# Test secure internal node\nsecure_node_ifaces = [{'name': 'ib0', 'ip': '10.240.1.15'}, {'name': 'lo', 'ip': '127.0.0.1'}]\nverdict_secure = controller.evaluate_node_admission('dgx-h100-node-01.bank.internal', secure_node_ifaces, verified_image)\n\n# Test rogue node with external internet interface\nrogue_node_ifaces = [{'name': 'eth0', 'ip': '198.51.100.44'}, {'name': 'lo', 'ip': '127.0.0.1'}]\nverdict_rogue = controller.evaluate_node_admission('untrusted-worker-09.external', rogue_node_ifaces, verified_image)\n\nprint(json.dumps({\n    'sovereign_node_admission_pass': asdict(verdict_secure),\n    'sovereign_node_admission_reject': asdict(verdict_rogue)\n}, indent=2))\n",
